let inGamut(<var>color</var>) be a function which returns true if, when passed a color,
		that color is inside the gamut of <var>destination</var>.
		For HSL and HWB, it returns true if the color is inside the gamut of sRGB.

let clip(<var>color</var>) be a function which converts <var>color</var> to <var>destination</var>,
		clamps each component to the bounds of the reference range for that component
		and returns the result

if the hue step from <var>samples</var>[<var>i</var> − 1]'s hue to <var>samples</var>[<var>i</var>]'s hue is forward,
				append <var>samples</var>[<var>i</var>] to <var>kept</var>, set <var>i</var> to <var>i</var> + 1,
				and continue with the next iteration

while <var>j</var> is less than the index of the last entry of <var>samples</var>,
				and the hue step from <var>samples</var>[<var>j</var>]'s hue to <var>samples</var>[<var>j</var> + 1]'s hue is not forward,
				set <var>j</var> to <var>j</var> + 1

